<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN>

<PLUGIN
  name="cloudflared"
  author="Daniel M. Matongo"
  version="2026.10.28"
  launch="Settings/Cloudflared"
  pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mmatongo/unraid-cloudflared/master/plugin/cloudflared.plg"
  support="https://github.com/mmatongo/unraid-cloudflared/issues"
  icon="cloudflared.png"
  min="6.11.5"
>

<CHANGES>
<![CDATA[
###2026.10.28###

- Self-contained plugin: the web UI files are embedded in the .plg (no more cloudflared-utils package, so no package checksum to maintain and no build/CI checksum mismatch).
- The cloudflared binary is no longer pinned in the .plg: scripts/cf-update.sh downloads the release from Cloudflare and checks its SHA256 against both the release notes and the digest computed by GitHub. Update with `cf-update.sh stage` then `cf-update.sh apply <version>`.
- Versioning change: the plugin version is now the plugin's own (date based), no longer the cloudflared version. Existing installs must be reinstalled once (Plugins > Install Plugin, or `plugin install <url> forced`); settings in /boot/config/plugins/cloudflared/config are kept.

###2026.7.1###

- Updated to version 2026.7.1

###2026.5.2###

- Updated to version 2026.5.2

###2025.9.1b###

- Updated to version 2025.9.1b
- Fix minor field issue

###2025.9.1a###

- Updated to version 2025.9.1a

###2025.6.1###

- Updated to version 2025.6.1

###2025.4.0###

- Updated to version 2025.4.0

###2025.2.1###

- Updated to version 2025.2.1

- minor changes

###2025.1.0b###

- Add support for empty TUNNEL_REGION

- Added changes to clean up old versions

###2025.1.0###

- Updated to version 2025.1.0

###2024.12.2a###

- Minor fixes

###2024.12.2###

- Updated to version 2024.12.2
- Fixed some issues around updating

###2024.11.11b###

- Bug fixes

###2024.11.11a###

- Bug fixes

###2024.11.11###
- Initial release with UI and service management

]]>
</CHANGES>

<!--
The 'install' script.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
log() {
    echo "$(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S') $1"
    logger -t cloudflared-install "$1"
}

verify_sha256() {
    local file="$1"
    local expected="$2"
    local actual=$(sha256sum "$file" | awk '{print $1}')
    if [ "$actual" != "$expected" ]; then
        log "SHA256 verification failed for $file"
        log "expected: $expected"
        log "got: $actual"
        return 1
    fi
    return 0
}

# Stop existing service if running
if [ -f "/var/run/cloudflared.pid" ]; then
    log "Stopping existing service..."
    /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/cloudflared/scripts/restart.sh stop
    sleep 2
fi

# Remove the old cloudflared-utils package of previous versions, then the plugin directory (clean install)
removepkg cloudflared-utils >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
if [ -d "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/cloudflared" ]; then
    log "Removing existing plugin installation..."
    rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/cloudflared
fi

]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

